                <pb facs="0461" n="363" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg363"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003/256: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Perkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-01-20T12:00:00+08:00">January 20,
                        1930—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received January 20—9 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>62. Legation’s 1201, Dec. 30, 9 a.m.,<anchor n="53" xml:id="d446-f1"/> and 6,
                    January 2, 5 p.m. Norwegian Chargé d’Affaires left yesterday for Nanking to
                    engage in extraterritoriality negotiations. Norwegian Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs informed British Minister in Oslo that the Norwegian Government was
                    prepared to follow the lead of the British Government in matters relating to the
                    relinquishment of extraterritorial rights.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
